ClientProfileView
*Updated 2026-10-12 to match the Harbor design (design/harbor/client/static/profile*.html). The design is the source of truth.*

is a form that allows the client to change their phone number, email, add a student, ~~remove a student,~~ pick a different profile picture (Phase 2)

*Design details:*
Your details:
  Your name, mobile phone, and email.
  Email: the family logs in with it. Changing it sends a code to the new address.
    *Decided 2026-10-12:* entering that code reuses the sign-up verify screen (signup-3-verify.html): 6-digit code,
    "Verify email", "Resend code" and "Use a different email". The old address stays the login until the code is
    entered (Cognito's keep-original-until-verified setting).
  "Text me reminders" switch, with the SMS terms (same as sign-up). *Phase 2 (2026-10-12): all client SMS deferred.*
  Profile picture: shown, with the Phase 2 tag; choosing one is disabled.

Skaters (everyone who takes lessons with the coach):
  Each skater with their name, under 18 or adult, organization and number, and "Approved" or "Waiting for approval".
  Add a skater: full name, under 18 yes or no, skating organization (U.S. Figure Skating, USA Hockey, or Learn to Skate USA since 2026-10-16) and number.
    The coach approves new skaters before they can be booked. No email is sent in MVP (see below). "Add skater" is disabled until
    the name and number are filled in.
  *More than one coach (2026-10-13, ADR-025 k):* adding a skater asks "Which coaches?" ~~; at least one must be ticked~~.
    *Changed 2026-11-06:* it always asks, and offers "None of my coaches yet" (see "Add a skater with no coach yet" below).
    The new skater waits for each coach picked.
  An adult who skates themselves can't add skaters: a child needs their own family account.
  Share code: each skater shows their share code with Copy. ~~New code~~ *Removed 2026-10-13: a skater's share
    code never changes and can't be refreshed (ADR-026, amended 2026-10-13).*
    Share codes are how lessons are shared: reference 'Schedule lesson split' for details.
  ~~Remove: asks for confirmation first.
    Approved skater: their upcoming lessons are cancelled and the coach is told; late cancellations may be charged.
    Waiting skater: the coach won't see the sign-up any more.~~
    *Removed 2026-10-13 by the owner: no Remove button on the family profile. What removing a skater means stays
    with the open "delete a student" decision (docs/Open-Pending.md).*

*More than one coach (2026-10-13; ADR-025 d2; profile-add-coach.html, profile-coach-sent.html):*
  Each skater lists their coaches: approved, or "Waiting for Coach <name>".
  Your coaches: each coach, their sport, and which skaters are with them (approved or waiting).
  Add a coach: enter the coach's code; the coach is shown to check it's the right one; tick which skaters join.
    Skaters already with that coach are shown but can't be ticked. Each skater then waits for that coach's
    approval alone; their other coaches aren't affected. To add a new skater, add them under Skaters first.
  Removing a skater from one coach doesn't affect their lessons with other coaches. Removing a skater
    is deferred with the "delete a student" question (owner, 2026-10-13); the profile has no Remove button.

Buttons: Save and Log out.

Waiting for approval: the same page. It's most of what a waiting family can see (ADR-022 d6).

  *ADR-002, amendment 2026-11-06 (owner): the approval email is Phase 2; MVP sends none. See Client Sign Up, "Coach
    approval".* *Ruled by the owner 2026-11-09.*

More than one coach, from ADR-025 (moved 2026-11-08):
  Adding a coach: from their account, a signed-in family can add a coach: enter that coach's code, then choose which
    skaters join them, existing ones or a new one. Each skater then waits for that coach's approval alone.
    *(from ADR-025 decision 2)*
  Phase 2 (owner, 2026-10-07), with "Also coached by" on the coach side: the add-a-coach screen tells the family
    "Coach Sam will see that Mia also skates with Coach Dana, and Coach Dana will see Coach Sam." The same line shows
    at sign-up when more than one coach is chosen. *(from ADR-025 decision 2 and its 2026-10-06 amendment)*
  k. *Decided by the owner 2026-10-13:* adding a skater on the profile asks which coaches they join (when the family has
    more than one). The new skater waits for each coach picked. *(from ADR-025, amendment 2026-10-13, item k)*
  n. Removing a skater from one coach or from all is Phase 2, with the rest of the "delete a student" question
    (blocker #17) (owner, 2026-10-13). *(from ADR-025, amendment 2026-10-13, item n)*

Add a skater with no coach yet (decided by the owner 2026-11-06, settling a conflict with the Harbor design,
design/harbor/client/screens-account.js, "To add a new skater, add them under Skaters first"):
  Item k changes: "Add a skater" always asks which coaches they join (now also when the family has only one coach)
    and offers "None of my coaches yet".
    *Ruled by the owner 2026-11-09.* The earlier "at least one must be ticked" is replaced.
  The profile then shows "Not with a coach yet", and the skater can't be booked, invited or added as a sibling.
  The family then uses "Add a coach", where the skater appears like any existing one.
  This avoids a new skater being made waiting with a coach they will never skate with, and that coach's decline email.
  Sign-up is unchanged: each skater still ticks at least one coach.
  The add-a-coach form keeps its hint, worded for the new path. The "None of my coaches yet" choice is drawn in
    design/harbor/client/ (profile-add-skater-no-coach, profile-add-skater-one-coach, profile-skater-no-coach,
    profile-add-coach-new-skater; 2026-11-06).
  *(from ADR-025, amendment 2026-11-06, moved 2026-11-08)*

Open questions (from ADR-025 Open, moved 2026-11-08):
  Designs for the new multi-coach screens, for about 10 coaches. Booking and the profile's coaches designed 2026-10-13,
    then sign-up, Home and the waiting pages the same day. Payments (Phase 2) is still to do; per-coach removal is
    Phase 2 (n). "Also coached by" on the coach side is Phase 2. 2026-11-06: the "None of my coaches yet" path is drawn
    too (four profile pages).
  What the family sees when one coach removes their skater while another coach keeps them. Part of blocker #17.
    2026-10-13: the other coaches' lessons aren't affected (ADR-025 g); what the family sees is still open, and
    Phase 2 with the rest of removal (n).
